dialect grammar
grammar forms.forms
extension forms
use family-scene
start document

# Real grammar for `FormsSnapshot::print_dsl`/`parse_dsl`
# (🚪️io/📸️snapshot/📝️text/🦀️component.rs's `print_forms_snapshot_body`/`parse_forms_snapshot_body`,
# lines 66-105) — a hand-rolled hex/bracket `key=value` line codec, one line per field, same
# convention `raster.document`/`playbook.playbook` use. This REPLACES the stale, cross-plugin
# copy-pasted "canvas layer" template (`layers { shape/path/text { canvas-field* } }`,
# `add-layer`/`set-stroke`/`move-layer`/`set-fill`) this file previously carried — see
# `.🧬semio/…/STUBS-AND-PLACEHOLDERS-COMPLETION/📓️grammar-envelope-transcription.md` for how that
# mismatch was discovered (forms is a step/block wizard, never a layered canvas).
#
# Note: the real preamble is `semio forms.form.dsl v1` — `FormsSnapshot::envelope_id()`
# (line 117-119) returns `crate::artifacts::forms::FORMS_DOCUMENT_SCHEMA`, whose own const value is
# `"forms.form"` (🦀️component.rs:16), NOT `"forms.forms"` — this grammar's own `grammar` header line
# is left untouched per the ticket brief (already corrected by a sibling agent), but the body below
# reflects the real runtime literal.
artifact-mark = "semio forms.form.dsl v1"
document = artifact-mark schema-line id-line version-line title-line structure-line results-line

schema-line = "schema" "=" hex
id-line = "id" "=" hex
version-line = "version" "=" hex
title-line = "title" "=" opt-hex
structure-line = "structure" "=" child-handle
results-line = "results" "=" child-handle

# `title`'s absent form is a bare `-`, NOT the `[0]`/`[1,...]` bracket convention
# `raster.document`/`playbook.playbook` use — a distinct hand-rolled `enc_opt_str` in this file.
opt-hex = "-" | hex
child-handle = "[" hex "," hex "]"

# `hex` (bare, deliberately not defined as a local production) is the framework's built-in `hex`
# macro — every hex-bracket-encoded leaf string is `enc_str` (lowercase-hex UTF-8 bytes).
